# TypeScript architecture

Canonical layout and contracts: technical guide §7–§8.

## Boundaries

- `src/domain` — pure state, policy, schemas; no React, Supabase client, or provider SDKs
- `src/server` — secrets, repositories, adapters, privileged commands
- `src/features` — compose domain into user flows
- `src/app` — routes/layouts; thin adapters only; call services, do not reimplement rules
- React components must not query privileged tables directly
- Provider SDK types must not leak into domain types
- Generated Supabase types: one generated file; never hand-edit

## Domain terms (do not mix)

`assessment_track`, `blueprint_version`, `practice_slot`, `booking`, `session`,
`session_participant`, `round`, `stage`, `transcript_segment`, `feedback_report`,
`product_event`, `domain_event`

Do not use `exam`, `test`, `session`, `match`, and `booking` interchangeably.

## Defaults

- Strict TypeScript; Zod at env, request, blueprint, and AI-output boundaries
- UUIDs for entities; opaque server-derived provider room names
- Every external mutation accepts or creates an idempotency key
- Prefer existing patterns; no overlapping form/validation/date/state/HTTP/UI libs
- Use `vercel-react-best-practices` and `vercel-composition-patterns` skills for React/Next code
